From 9e916868edcec75548e869ce7e835802464a0967 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 731/731] perf(dsv41): exchange WO-A MXFP8 rows and project
 WO-B on local SP rows

Under sequence-parallel prefill on encoder attention layers, run WO-A once on
all T rows into its native MXFP8 (xq, sf) buffers, exchange those narrower
o_lora rows across ranks while projecting this rank's own WO-B shard on the L
local rows, and project each peer rank's WO-B shard on the L local rows into
parts ([world, L, 5120] BF16).

This cuts per-layer SP WO collective payload by 69.06% on TP3 Ranks 0/1 and
79.38% on TP3 Rank 2 (72.50% cluster-wide average) and by 79.38% on TP4 across
all 20 encoder layers, while eliminating repeated per-slice/per-owner WO-A and
WO-B weight re-reads.

Upstream base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354
Immediate base: c47b54ae471a24b830e3515212b8c0bf5ee14604
Quality: bit-identical to the full-row SP WO path across all finite, signed-zero,
and non-finite inputs; no precision or rounding change anywhere.
Tests: tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_attention.py,
tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_sp_prefill.py, and
tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_l2_schedule.py.
Upstream status: local DeepSeek-V4.1 sequence-parallel prefill optimization.
